      $\boldsymbol{\tau}_j$ and $\mathbf{W}_b$ are the JTSs and base F/T sensor measurements, respectively. Utilizing the robot states
      ($\tilde{\mathbf{x}}$) and contact information ($\tilde{\mathbf{r}}_{c,i}$ and $\tilde{\boldsymbol{\lambda}}_i$), the contact-feedback MPC
      calculates $\mathbf{X}^*$ and $\mathbf{U}^*$. Then, $\mathbf{u}^{[0]*}$ is commanded to the torque-controlled robot.
    </div>
